+section('troubleshooting', 'Troubleshooting', 'life-preserver')
  //- `…` in a question or answer marks a command or parameter: rendered as
  //- <code>, with everything else HTML-escaped first (so `<instance>` shows as text).
  -
    const faq = [
      ['A Client doesn\'t appear on Runners', 'Check `journalctl -u thub-client@<instance> -f`. A `503` at registration means the Coordinator has no `clientJoinKey`; a `401` means the `joinKey` differs. Also check that `coordinatorUrl` is reachable from the lab (`curl -sI <url>/login`).'],
      ['A Client flaps or two machines show as one runner', 'Both use the same `.client-id` (a cloned VM or a shared config file). Delete `<varDir>/<instance>/.client-id` on one of them and restart it, or set a distinct `clientId`.'],
      ['Name already in use (`409`)', 'Another live Client holds that name. Rename one of them in its config or from the runner card. A name held by an `OUT_OF_SERVICE` runner is reclaimed automatically.'],
      ['The job is rejected with `422`', 'No registered Client can ever match its type, labels, group or client. Compare `thub resources` with your `--type` and `--label`s; your group (set on the dashboard, see `thub whoami`) must have a Client of that kind.'],
      ['The job stays `QUEUED`', 'Matching Clients are all `BUSY`, locked (`local`), in `MAINTENANCE` or offline, or the job is pinned with `--client`. It times out after `--timeout`.'],
      ['`ERROR` during prepare', 'The clone, download or DUT image pull failed; the job log names the reason. For git, check the Client user\'s keys and `known_hosts` (`ssh -T git@<host>` as that user). For images, check the Client user\'s `docker login`.'],
      ['Permission denied on `/dev/ttyUSB*` or `docker.sock`', 'Docker or the device groups were added after the Client was installed. Re-run `sudo npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-client` so the unit gets the `dialout`/`plugdev`/`docker` groups, then restart.'],
      ['A configured device is shown as missing', 'Check the `devpath` with `udevadm info -a -n <dev>`, then `thub-client udev --print`; restart the Client to regenerate the udev rules.'],
      ['Job `LOST`', 'The Client missed 3 heartbeats (network, reboot, crash). With `requeueOnLost` the job is retried once on another Client.'],
      ['A job can\'t write to `~` (read-only file system)', 'Under systemd the Client can only write to its state directory. Write to `$THUB_WORK_DIR`, and set `DOCKER_CONFIG` there for `docker login`.'],
      ['Live logs don\'t stream through the proxy', 'Turn off response buffering for the Coordinator (nginx: `proxy_buffering off;`, Caddy: `flush_interval -1`).'],
      ['Finding a job, runner, group or agent', 'Use the search box on its list page (press `/` to jump to it). Every word must match, e.g. `lab-hw-01 FAILED` or a git ref. Job search covers ids, users, runners, agents, commands, repos and `--meta`, but not `--env` values (secrets). On a job page, search the log above the log viewer: `Enter`/`Shift+Enter` step through matches.'],
      ['Lists don\'t update by themselves (navbar shows Offline or Paused)', '`Paused`: you\'re editing something on the page (a field, the inline rename, a dialog); it resumes when you\'re done. `Offline`: the browser can\'t hold the `/live` stream open, often a proxy buffering it (nginx: `proxy_buffering off;`); reloading the page always shows current data. `Session ended`: sign in again. Background updates never extend the session\'s idle timeout.'],
      ['Sign-in says it needs HTTPS', 'The session cookie is HTTPS-only because `publicUrl` is `https://`, but the request arrived as plain HTTP. Open the dashboard through its https:// address; behind a reverse proxy, make it send `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` (nginx: `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;`) and check `trustProxy`. To allow plain HTTP, set `session.secureCookie` to `false`.'],
      ['Where are a job\'s test reports and output files?', 'The Coordinator keeps only the log and the result (verdict, exit code, JUnit test counts). Files the job creates stay in its workspace on the Client and are deleted when the job ends. To keep them, publish them from `--command`, e.g. `curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $ART_TOKEN" -T results/report.xml "https://artifactory.example.com/qa/$THUB_JOB_ID/report.xml"` with `--env ART_TOKEN`. To show them on the job page and in `thub status`, list them in `$THUB_ARTIFACTS_FILE` as `[{"name", "size", "link", "timestamp"}]` — only that metadata is kept. The full log is always available from the job page\'s Raw button.'],
      ['429 Too Many Requests', 'A caller went over `rateLimit.requestsPerMinute` (per agent or runner token, per dashboard user, else per IP; default 500). The Agent and Client wait for `Retry-After` and retry by themselves; a script calling the API should do the same. Raise the limit in the config file or on Settings if your normal traffic needs more (a Client streaming logs makes up to ~240 requests a minute). Too many sign-in attempts from one address: wait a minute (`rateLimit.loginPerMinute`).'],
      ['Sign-in says “Too many failed sign-ins”', 'After repeated wrong passwords the Coordinator makes each further attempt wait, doubling each time: per address from the 5th failure (up to 15 min), per username from the 10th from any address (up to 5 min). Wait the time shown, or sign in from another address; a successful sign-in clears it, and an hour without failures forgets it. The Coordinator never tells whether a username exists.'],
      ['Agent says “Invalid or revoked access key” or “… is blocked”', 'The key was replaced (`thub key rotate`, an admin, your profile) or revoked, or your user is blocked. Ask an admin for a new key (Users), or create one on your profile if you can sign in. Then `thub config set key <key>`; `thub whoami` checks it.'],
      ['The Coordinator won\'t start after an upgrade: `SqliteError: disk I/O error` (`SQLITE_IOERR_GETTEMPPATH`)', 'Its systemd unit is older than 1.1.1: it has `ProtectSystem=strict` without `PrivateTmp=yes`, so SQLite has no writable temp directory for a large migration. The migration rolls back, so no data is lost. Install the latest version with `sudo npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-coordinator` (the dashboard can\'t update a Coordinator that\'s down), or run `sudo systemctl edit thub-coordinator`, add `[Service]` and `PrivateTmp=yes`, then `sudo systemctl restart thub-coordinator`.'],
      ['Locked out of the dashboard', 'Restart the Coordinator once with `THUB_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<new>` (resets the `admin` user), then unset it.']
    ]
    const withCode = (text) => text
      .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
      .replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>')
  .accordion#help-faq
    each item, i in faq
      .accordion-item
        h3.accordion-header
          button.accordion-button.collapsed.small(
            type="button"
            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
            data-bs-target=`#faq-${i}`
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls=`faq-${i}`
          )
            //- One inline box: .accordion-button is flex, which would drop
            //- the spaces around <code>.
            span!= withCode(item[0])
        .accordion-collapse.collapse(id=`faq-${i}` data-bs-parent="#help-faq")
          .accordion-body.small!= withCode(item[1])
  p.small.text-body-secondary.mt-3.mb-0.
    The full design reference (API, state machines, database schema) is in the project README. Everything
    that happens is also recorded per job: open it from #[a(href="/jobs") Jobs] for its spec, timeline and log.
